 ## Background
-Forward Warping for Novel View Synthesis was proposed in the paper "Forward Flow for Novel View Synthesis of Dynamic Scenes" [S1]. The method builds on the idea of canonical representations but introduces forward warping with average splatting and an inpaint network to handle dynamic scenes. It was evaluated on the D-NeRF and HyperNeRF datasets, as well as a newly built Lego Complete Dataset [S1].
+Forward Warping for Novel View Synthesis was proposed in the paper "Forward Flow for Novel View Synthesis of Dynamic Scenes" [S1]. It builds on the canonical field representation approach, addressing limitations of backward flow methods by explicitly warping the canonical field forward in time. The method was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China and other grants [S1].
 
